        "original_id": "ceb63600-8b91-596e-a460-3bb17170ea28",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Topics: Cinema of Ukraine, historical Armenia\n- People: Oleksandr Dovzhenko, Dzyha Vertov, Serhiy Paradzhanov\n- Places: Ukraine, Armenia, Turkey, Georgia\n- Concepts: Ukrainian poetic cinema, socialist realism\n\nFacts:\n- Ukraine has had an influence on the history of cinema.\n- Oleksandr Dovzhenko, Dzyha Vertov, and Serhiy Paradzhanov are prominent directors in the cinema of Ukraine.\n- Serhiy Paradzhanov was an Armenian film director and artist who made significant contributions to Ukrainian, Armenian, and Georgian cinema.\n- Serhiy Paradzhanov invented his own cinematic style, Ukrainian poetic cinema, which was out of step with the guiding principles of socialist realism.\n- The Republic of Armenia constitutes only one-tenth of historical Armenia.\n- Most of historical Armenia is currently occupied by Turkey.",
